 [Dawn] Re: Updated draft-dunbar-dawn-infra-assisted-discovery\nL33: List-Id: \"The list is for discussion of the scope, use cases, requirements, and solutions for discovery of entities (e.g., tasks, AI agents, or endpoints) using IETF technologies.\" <dawn.ietf.org>\nL34: Archived-At: <https://mailarchive.ietf.org/arch/msg/dawn/Quse3xqhbag1_uoXRjrxXIPLypE>\nL35: List-Archive: <https://mailarchive.ietf.org/arch/browse/dawn>\nL36: List-Help: <mailto:dawn-request@ietf.org?subject=help>\nL37: List-Owner: <mailto:dawn-owner@ietf.org>\nL38: List-Post: <mailto:dawn@ietf.org>\nL39: List-Subscribe: <mailto:dawn-join@ietf.org>\nL40: List-Unsubscribe: <mailto:dawn-leave@ietf.org>\nL41: \nL42:     Linda,\nL43: \nL44:     I reviewed the -03 and have a couple of comments on Caching and Freshness\nL45:     (8.6) and No Result (8.7).\nL46: \nL47:        1. *Held Discovery Information:* 8.6 says DNS information obtained\nL48:        earlier may still be cached when the requester's Attachment Scope changes,\nL49:        and that a new discovery should use the current context. The Attachment\nL50:        Scope doesn't need to be exposed to the requester (5.3), so it doesn't see\nL51:        its own scope change and nothing prompts that new discovery. Until the TTL\nL52:        runs out, it keeps using what it got under the old scope.\nL53:        2. *No Result Versus Error:* 8.7 lets a deployment move a subsequent\nL54:        bootstrap operation to a broader scope when one fails to obtain discovery\nL55:        information. DNS-SD's no-result and error indications both count as that\nL56:        failure. A timeout says nothing about whether the edge-local scope has an\nL57:        instance, so falling back on it can hand the requester a less applicable\nL58:        resource.\nL59: \nL60:     We should say in 8.6 that information obtained under an Attachment Scope\nL61:     holds only while that scope holds, and in 8.7 that the fallback follows a\nL62:     complete no-result answer, kept apart from an error.\nL63: \nL64:     Thanks,\nL65:     Girish\nL66: \nL67:     On Sat, Oct 31, 2026 at 10:52 PM Александр Артамохов <alexar76=\nL68:     40rambler.ru@dmarc.ietf.org> wrote:\nL69: \nL70:     > Hi Linda,\nL71:     >\nL72:     > Thank's for the update.\nL73:     >\nL74:     > The clear boundary in -03 is helpful: bootstrap discovery returns the\nL75:     > minimum needed to reach an agent, while catalog search, ranking and\nL76:     > cost-based selection stay out of scope.\nL77:     > That excluded part is what draft-artamokhov-dawn-marketplace-discovery\nL78:     > addresses: how a requester finds catalogs (marketplaces) that list agents\nL79:     > and tools across operators, through a well-known URI, before any selection\nL80:     > happens.\nL81:     > The two seem complementary: your model finds an entry point inside a\nL82:     > managed network, and a catalog is used when the requester has to search\nL83:     > beyond it.\nL84:     >\nL85:     > One question: should the metadata reference returned by bootstrap\nL86:     > discovery be allowed to point to such a catalog, or do you see catalogs as\nL87:     > entirely separate from bootstrap discovery?\nL88:     >\nL89:     > Best regards, Aleksandr Artamokhov\nL90:     >\nL91:     > 01.11.2026, 05:47, Linda Dunbar <\nL92:     > linda.dunbar=40futurewei.com@dmarc.ietf.org>\nL93:     >\nL94:     > Hi all,\nL95:     >\nL96:     >\nL97:     > Thanks to Adrian for the detailed comments, and to everyone for the\nL98:     > helpful discussion on the DAWN mailing list.\nL99:     >\nL100:     >\nL101:     > We have updated draft\nL102:     > 【0†https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-dunbar-dawn-infra-assisted-discovery/†datatracker.ietf.org】\nL103:     > . The revision aligns the terminology more closely with the DAWN\nL104:     > terminology draft, in particular around MVD/MDI and the role of requester\nL105:     > context. It also clarifies that the infrastructure-assisted model supports\nL106:     > bootstrap discovery by contributing current resource state and requester\nL107:     > context, without defining registration, catalog search, semantic\nL108:     > matchmaking, ranking, or resource selection.\nL109:     >\nL110:     >\nL111:     > The updated draft also distinguishes more clearly between DAWN bootstrap\nL112:     > discovery and subsequent retrieval of richer agent-native metadata such as\nL113:     > an A2A Agent Card.\nL114:     >\nL115:     >\nL116:     > Comments and suggestions are very welcome.\nL117:     >\nL118:     >\nL119:     > Best regards,\nL120:     >\nL121:     > Linda\nL122:     >\nL123:     >\nL124:     >\nL125:     >\nL126:     >\nL127:     >\nL128:     >\nL129:     >\nL130:     >\nL131:     >\nL132:     >\nL133:     >\nL134:     >\nL135:     > _______________________________________________\nL136:     > Dawn mailing list -- dawn@ietf.org <http:///compose>\nL137:     > To unsubscribe send an email to dawn-leave@ietf.org <http:///compose>\nL138:     >\nL139:     > _______________________________________________\nL140:     > Dawn mailing list -- dawn@ietf.org\nL141:     > To unsubscribe send an email to dawn-leave@ietf.org\nL142:     >\nL143:   * 【1†[Dawn] Updated draft-dunbar-dawn-infra-assisted-d…】  Linda Dunbar\nL144:   * 【2†[Dawn] Re: Updated draft-dunbar-dawn-infra-assist…】  Александр Артамохов\nL145:   * 【3†[Dawn] Re: Updated draft-dunbar-dawn-infra-assist…】  Girish Konda\nL146: \nL147:   * 【4†Hide Navigation Bar】\nL148: \nL149: Date\nL150: \nL151: Thread\nL152: \nL153: v2.46.0 | 【5†Report a Bug†github.com】 | By Email (tools-help@ietf.org) | 【6†System Status†status.ietf.org】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[Dawn] Re: Updated draft-dunbar-dawn-infra-assisted-discovery (https://mailarchive.ietf.org/arch/msg/dawn/R1Ga6qDX0E2jy7aHNWkeyAsu2AM/)\nciteturn84view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 days ago; Content type: text/html; Source: click({\"ref_id\":\"turn82view0\",\"id\":4}); T